li-i-p2 = prose (cons "DSM-5 states that socially deviant behavior, and conflict primarily between the individual and society, is not a mental disorder unless it results from a dysfunction in the individual. It defines a delusion as a fixed belief not amenable to change in light of conflicting evidence. Grandiosity is self-esteem inflated relative to reality. Every one of these terms is a relation between a belief and the world. None has content until the relation is established: a delusion is a falsehood (de-ludere, to play false), and a falsehood must be shown." nil)
